---
name: ui-finalize
description: "Assemble a truthful, reproducible delivery for the completed Studio scope. Use after design-only or production work to verify artifacts, decisions, costs, packaging and remaining limitations."
---

# Finalize the requested scope

Implementation target: activate with compatible Studio commands.

## Inputs and scope

Read the run's actual stage/scope, committed artifact/component versions, applicable decisions, acceptance receipts, installation/package targets and budget ledger. Distinguish design-only delivery from production/release completion.

## Workflow

Verify the deliverable inventory and exact dependency versions. Check that selected decisions remain applicable and required gates cover the delivered build. Reconcile known cost outcomes; expose unresolved charges/reservations rather than treating them as settled.

For packaged delivery, verify included references, install/upgrade/restore behaviour and supported host integration from actual evidence. Preserve aliases and documented migration. Use the applicable requirements and gates; do not load all source books.

Confirm the user can open the real artifacts and follow a practical next step. Record limitations, failed/blocked/deferred checks and recovery information alongside results.

## Mode, outputs and exit

Guided and YOLO share the same evidence standard. User decisions and agent decisions retain their real actor. Finalization itself does not authorize external publication, merge or a new purchase.

Return artifact/version inventory, decision history, cost summary, checks, known risks and the next valid action. State human participant research is deferred where relevant. A pack-integrity pass does not establish implementation; an automated pass does not establish human usability.

Exit successfully only when the requested scope's acceptance conditions are satisfied. Otherwise preserve the concrete deliverable and report the precise remaining blocker without calling the product complete.
